article en "Explicit Doc source archive v1"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons code "nepl3.doc-archive"
      cons text " revision 1 defines "
      cons code "DocumentArchive"
      cons text " with ordered fields "
      cons code "skeleton: nepl3.doc/1 DocumentSyntax"
      cons text " and "
      cons code "group: Bytes"
      cons text "."
      nil
    cons " The latter is a checked GroupArchive/1 byte stream."
    cons " The JSON contract and Rust descriptor are compared by the repository contract checker, including the Doc/Foundation dependency closure."
    cons " The host must also register the source/group archive contracts required by its explicit archive codec."
    cons " Missing contracts reject; they never select a v1 fallback."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "This is an opt-in transport API."
    cons " Existing DocumentSyntax, PageSet, preparation, HTML, Text and Print APIs, operation domains and descriptor identities are unchanged."
    cons " The ordinary FoundationValueCodec trait remains usable without archive support."
    cons " The optional FoundationGroupArchiveCodec capability has a real concrete wire implementation and no success-shaped default."
    cons " It shares its ordinary codec's registry, SourceAdmission and cumulative Budget."
    cons " Schema capability selection is codec boundary work; once selected, group encoding preserves caller-relative semantic depths and checks a distinct codec registry independently."
    nil
  cons section encoding "Encoding"
  body
    cons paragraph
      cons "Prepare the original native Doc structure and its maximum occurrence depth for each shared embed."
      cons " Encode that exact group through the depth-aware compact Foundation operation, retaining GroupArchive bytes and ordered v2 guest component commitments."
      cons " A provider result with a different component count rejects."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Encode the otherwise unchanged Doc value with an empty Foundation group at the typed DocEmbeds.group field."
      cons " Preserve embed kinds and references, document sources, origins, views and mappings."
      cons " Validate the skeleton structurally as DocumentSyntax, then validate the complete DocumentArchive envelope before returning it."
      cons " The skeleton is not independently valid native Doc syntax when it contains embeds."
      cons " It does not replace the original native validation or prove render readiness."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence
        cons text "The returned guest components are the v2 Foundation entry commitments defined in "
        cons link relative "27-group-source-archive.md" none text "the group archive contract"
        cons text "."
        nil
      cons " No new document or preparation-plan identity is defined by this transport API."
      nil
    nil
  cons section decoding "Decoding"
  body
    cons paragraph
      cons "Validate the explicit envelope and its Doc skeleton against their selected registry identities."
      cons " Decode GroupArchive bytes into a native group, restoring and validating every local source declaration set."
      cons " Decode the document's own source scope using the same admission ledger; conflicting document/guest identities reject."
      cons " A globally admitted declaration cannot fill a missing local set."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Private generated typed reader hooks restore DocValue.embeds and DocEmbeds.group without expanding the native group back into v1 NDF."
      cons " All ordinary fields retain the existing read order and Work charges."
      cons " The placeholder group must be empty in all three tables; a nonempty placeholder rejects."
      cons " Opaque group payloads are not rewritten."
      cons " Origins, mappings and views retain the existing document-local scope."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Finally validate the complete restored native Doc structure, including the maximum depth of each shared embed across shallow/deep owner paths under the active outer Budget depth."
      cons " Successful GroupArchive decoding alone cannot discharge this Doc requirement."
      cons " Wrong archive/source membership, missing declarations, incompatible registries and malformed native values reject before a document is returned."
      nil
    nil
  cons section resource "Resource and acceptance scope"
  body
    cons paragraph
      cons "All descriptor lookup, capture, validation, allocation, canonical encoding, hashing, restoration and Doc validation use the supplied Budget."
      cons " Caller-side raw NDF serialization/deserialization must use that same budget for a single composite boundary operation."
      cons " Stops retain their reason and consumed usage; no successful partial document or archive is returned."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Native/CBOR roundtrip, alternate codec parity, unchanged v1 boundaries, route mismatch, empty groups, nonempty placeholders, source conflicts, deepest shared occurrence, provider cardinality, cancellation and exact/one-short budgets are transport acceptance requirements."
      cons " This milestone does not select a compact PageSet/preparation/rendering route or establish real-data generation under 4B Work."
      nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence
        cons text "Page-set structural transport is specified separately in "
        cons link relative "29-doc-pages-source-archive.md" none text "Doc PageSet archive"
        cons text "."
        nil
      nil
    nil
  nil
